{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>And the earth produced.</b> Produce in the seven years of plenty. The language of 'making' here is language of abundance, and it comes to teach that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded the blessing upon the grain; for we find the language of 'making' in connection with grain, as it is said (Leviticus 25): ״וצויתי את ברכתי לכם״ and so on, ״ועשת את התבואה״." "<b>Into storehouses.</b> Like לגמצים, from the language of (Ecclesiastes 10:8) ״חופר גומץ״, for excavations made in the ground are called קמצים, since the letters קו\"ף and גימ\"ל interchange among the letters גיכ\"ק. And likewise (II Samuel 15) ״ויציקו את ארון האלהים״, like ויציגו from the language of ״והצגתיו לפניך״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {1 "Verse citations normalized: Ecclesiastes 10:8 (not numbered in source); II Samuel 15:24 (reference abbreviated as chapter 15 only)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:37.719246112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}